      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-108429",
      ":question/problem": "Let $\u0393(\u03b1, \u03bb)$ denote the gamma distribution with shape parameter $\u03b1$ and rate parameter $\u03bb$. Given that $X\u223c\u0393(5, 2)$, express $P(X < 4)$ as an integral.\n\n*Hint: A gamma random variable $X\u223c\u0393(\u03b1, \u03bb)$ with shape parameter $\u03b1$ and rate parameter $\u03bb$ has the following probability density function:*\n\n$f(x) = {(\u03bb^{\u03b1})/(\u0393(\u03b1))x^{\u03b1 - 1}e^{- \u03bbx},\\begin{vmatrix}x > 0 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$\n*where $\u0393(\u03b1)$ is the gamma function.*"
